Need check `glowTexture` radial gradient function uses inner.replace regex; inner string "rgba(255,255,255,1)" -> replace `[\d.]+\)$` with '0.75)' gives "rgba(255,255,255,0.75)" good. If inner hex? default only. Fine.
Potential shader attribute `color` not declared? Built-in ShaderMaterial does not automatically declare color unless `vertexColors`? In custom shader, we use `color` attribute but didn't declare `attribute vec3 color;`. For ShaderMaterial, built-in attributes position, normal, uv are prepended; `color` is not unless vertexColors true. We set geometry attr but need `vertexColors: true` or declare attribute. In ShaderMaterial, `vertexColors` flag may add define but not declaration? Actually WebGLProgram prefix includes `attribute vec3 color;` only if `vertexColors` true? Let's recall three.js ShaderMaterial: default vertex shader prefix includes attribute position, normal, uv, uv1, uv2, color? WebGLProgram builds prefix based on parameters.vertexColors? For ShaderMaterial, vertexColors sets `#define USE_COLOR` and prefix includes `attribute vec3 color;` maybe. Safer declare `attribute vec3 color;` explicitly. But if prefix also declares, duplicate error. Hmm. Three r160 WebGLProgram vertex prefix includes:
```
attribute vec3 position;
attribute vec3 normal;
attribute vec2 uv;
#ifdef USE_TANGENT ...
#if defined( USE_COLOR_ALPHA )
 attribute vec4 color;
#elif defined( USE_COLOR ) || defined( USE_INSTANCING_COLOR )
 attribute vec3 color;
#endif
```
So with vertexColors:true defines USE_COLOR. Add `vertexColors: true` to ShaderMaterial. Then color attribute declared by prefix. Let's patch.

